#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:1
msgid "ROS 2 Interoperability"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:3
msgid ""
"`rrbot` is a simple two-link robotic arm with revolute joints, and this "
"tutorial serves as an illustrative example using the same to demonstrate the "
"interoperability of ROS 2 and Gazebo Sim."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:5
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "概覽"

#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:6
msgid ""
"We'll leverage ROS 2's communication and control mechanisms to interact with "
"the robot. Gazebo is used as the simulation environment, providing realistic "
"physics simulation and visualization of the `rrbot` robot arm. The robot "
"model is described using [SDFormat](http://sdformat.org/) (Simulation "
"Description Format), which defines the robot's structure, joints, links, and "
"their properties. While Gazebo's physics engine simulates the dynamics of "
"the robot, [RViz](https://github.com/ros2/rviz), a visualization tool in ROS "
"2, displays the robot model and its motion based on data published by the "
"control nodes, all using the same robot description file. Users can interact "
"with `rrbot` through ROS 2 commands to move the robot's arms or retrieve "
"joint state information."
msgstr ""

