#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:61
msgid ""
"Now if you'd want to extend this to visualize robot motion, we need "
"positions and transforms. The [`robot_state_publisher`](https://github.com/"
"ros/robot_state_publisher) takes the description and joint angles of the "
"robot as inputs and publishes the 3D poses of the robot links, using a "
"kinematic tree model of the robot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:63
msgid ""
"robot_state_publisher = Node(\n"
"    package='robot_state_publisher',\n"
"    executable='robot_state_publisher',\n"
"    name='robot_state_publisher',\n"
"    output='both',\n"
"    parameters=[\n"
"        {'use_sim_time': True},\n"
"        {'robot_description': robot_desc},\n"
"    ]\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:75
msgid ""
"These 3D poses are published on the `/tf` topic which is useful to track/"
"plan the robot's motion, communicate between different parts of the robot or "
"evaluate the robot's performance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:77
msgid "Configure a communication bridge"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_interop.md:79
msgid ""
"These joint states can either come from `joint_state_publisher` as seen "
"earlier or from simulated [JointStatePub](https://gazebosim.org/api/sim/10/"
"classgz_1_1sim_1_1systems_1_1JointStatePublisher.html) system's "
